   Known Limitation: Narrative Section Heading Depth (Item 1 "Business")

- Issue: In narrative sections (e.g., Apple 2016 Item 1 "Business"), certain sub-topics share identical font styling with their sibling items or render as plain body text (e.g., "iOS", "macOS", "Services"). 
- Cause: `heading_detector.py` relies strictly on visual font signals rather than NLP/semantic analysis, making it unable to detect conceptual hierarchy changes when styling is identical.
- Impact: Zero data loss. All text is fully preserved in paragraph content and retrievable via vector embeddings. The sub-topics are simply absorbed into the nearest parent heading node instead of forming independent heading nodes.
- Scope: Audited 13 L4-heading clusters across Apple 2016 10-K; only 1 cluster ("Products" on p. 5) exhibited this ambiguity. Confirmed as an isolated edge case per Section 7 triage rules.




